<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Murut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Murut are an Indigenous people of the interior of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>, mainly in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a> in Malaysia and neighbouring parts of Sarawak, Kalimantan and Brunei. Traditionally hill <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> farmers and hunters living in longhouses, they practised headhunting until the early 20th century. In 1915 the Murut leader Ontoros Antanom led a rising against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-north-borneo-company">British North Borneo Company</a>.</p></div>
